# Pin line endings by file type so platform-native wrappers/scripts don't
# show up as spuriously "modified" when an editor or tool re-flips CRLF<->LF.
# Surgical on purpose: only wrapper/script types are governed here, to avoid a
# repo-wide renormalization. `text eol=crlf` stores LF in the repo and checks
# out CRLF in the working tree (correct for Windows batch); `eol=lf` keeps
# unix scripts LF everywhere.

*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
mvnw   text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
